------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party / derived code
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of this software, in particular the autonomy pipeline under
`examples/av_pipeline/pipeline/` (objects, camera, detection, perception,
prediction, planning, control) and the helpers under
`examples/av_pipeline/utils/`, are DERIVED FROM and MODIFIED versions of code
from:

    ERDOS Pylot
    https://github.com/erdos-project/pylot
    Copyright The ERDOS / Pylot Authors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

The code was re-structured into a standalone Python package, de-coupled from
the ERDOS dataflow runtime, had import paths and hard-coded filesystem paths
changed, and had unused code paths removed. These modifications are likewise
released under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Each derived module also says so
in its own docstring.

    NOT derived: the staged-pipeline machinery under `cadet/pipeline/` is
    original CADET code and shares nothing but a directory name with the
    autonomy pipeline above. An earlier revision of this file named
    `cadet/pipeline/` as the derived path, which was true before the derived
    code was moved to `examples/av_pipeline/` and is why the distinction is
    spelled out here.

The network-emulation backend under `cadet/network/netwaggle/` is an ADAPTED
version of the approach and implementation of:

    NetWaggle / IoCT-Testbed-Simulation
    https://github.com/nesl/IoCT-Testbed-Simulation
    Copyright The NESL IoCT Testbed Authors

It was restructured from a single operator-driven script into a library with an
explicit lifecycle (build/start/stop/status) and no blocking CLI on the default
path; process handling was corrected to use real process handles; an unshaped
bypass interface per emulated host was added so framework plumbing does not
cross the emulated network; link shaping was extended to per-direction delay,
jitter, loss and bandwidth; and teardown was made bounded and self-cleaning.

    The upstream repository carries no license file. Redistribution terms for
    this adaptation are to be settled with its authors.

This project also relies on separately-licensed external components that are
NOT included here and retain their own licenses, including the CARLA simulator
and its PythonAPI, the SORT and DeepSORT trackers, and the Frenet Optimal
Trajectory planner. See each project for its respective license terms.
